; evil_crash_udf.def
; Windows DLL export table for tests\evil_crash_udf.c, gate 06's
; deliberately self-crashing MySQL UDF. MySQL's CREATE FUNCTION ...
; SONAME resolves the UDF's entry points via GetProcAddress on the
; plugin DLL, but MSVC exports NO plain C symbols from a /LD build by
; default (unlike a Linux gcc -shared .so, which exports everything --
; which is why build_test.sh's own use of this same file needs no
; export table at all). Without this table, CREATE FUNCTION fails
; "Can't find function 'bt_evil_crash' in library", gate 06's SELECT
; fails ERROR 1305, no crash ever happens, and the gate's respawn/data-
; integrity assertions pass for the wrong reason. Same .def technique
; as tests\windows\fractalsql-test-plugin.def (the reasoning-VFS-ABI
; fixtures); this is a separate table because that one exports the
; plugin-ABI symbol fsql_reasoning_init, while a UDF exports the three
; MySQL UDF entry points below.

EXPORTS
    bt_evil_crash
    bt_evil_crash_init
    bt_evil_crash_deinit